Top-down dungeon map, dark fantasy style, ink and parchment aesthetic. Deep underground level, total darkness except for player light sources. Five rooms. Room 1: circular chamber with domed ceiling, well shaft opening in center ceiling with dangling basket on rope, puddle beneath. Room 2: very long straight corridor (60ft), low ceiling, the first half has dust and debris on floor, the second half is suspiciously clean and polished (Gelatinous Cube territory), a few coins and rat skeletons seem to float in mid-air in the clean section (suspended inside transparent cube). Room 3: small square antechamber, completely empty, single sturdy wooden door on far wall. Room 4: rectangular cell, walls completely covered in charcoal drawings (portraits, landscapes, a recurring woman's face), a thin bearded man sitting against the wall, basket hanging from ceiling hole (well shaft from above). Cold blue-black palette with warm spots only where light sources are placed. Wet stone textures. Grid overlay 5ft squares. No text, no labels.
